{
  "title": "40: al-Ghaafir غافر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nحٰمٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa Mim \nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL AL-A’ALEEME.\nThe revelation of this Book is from Allah, Exalted in Power, Full of Knowledge, \nغَافِرِ الذَّنْۢبِ وَقَابِلِ التَّوْبِ شَدِيْدِ الْعِقَابِ ذِى الطَّوْلِؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَؕ اِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(3)\nGHAAFERE AZ-ZANBE WAQAABELE AT-TAWBE SHADEEDE E’QAAB ZIL AT-TAWLE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO ELAYHE MASEER.\nWho forgiveth sin, accepteth repentance, is strict in punishment, and hath a long reach (in all things). there is no god but He: to Him is the final goal. \nمَا يُجَادِلُ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَلَا يَغْرُرْكَ تَقَلُّبُهُمْ فِى الْبِلَادِ‏(4)\nMAA YUJAADELU FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE ILLAL LAZEENA KAFAROO FALAA YAGHRURKA TAQALLUBUHUM FIL BELAADE.\nNone can dispute about the Signs of Allah but the Unbelievers. Let not, then, their strutting about through the land deceive thee! \nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ وَهَمَّتْ كُلُّ اُمَّةٍۢ بِرَسُوْلِهِمْ لِيَاْخُذُوْهُ ؕ وَجَادَلُوْا بِالْبَاطِلِ لِيُدْحِضُوْا بِهِ الْحَقَّ فَاَخَذْتُهُمْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عِقَابِ‏(5)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WA YAATIL MIN BA’DEHIM WAHAMMAT KULLO UMMATIN BERASOOLEHEM LEEAKHUZOOHU WAJAADALOOA BIL-BAATELE LEEDHEZOOA BEHIL HAQQA FAAKHAZTUHUM FA-KAYFA KAANA E’EQAABE.\nBut (there were people) before them, who denied (the Signs), the People of Noah, and the Confederates (of Evil) after them; and every People plotted against their prophet, to seize him, and disputed by means of vanities, therewith to condemn the Truth; but it was I that seized them! and how (terrible) was My Requital! \nوَكَذٰلِكَ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؔ‌ۘ‏(6)\nWA KAZAALEKA HAQQAT KALEMATU RABBEKA A’LAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAHUM ASHAABUN NAAR.\nThus was the Decree of thy Lord proved true against the Unbelievers; that truly they are Companions of the Fire! \nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَحْمِلُوْنَ الْعَرْشَ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهٗ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا‌ ۚ رَبَّنَا وَسِعْتَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ رَّحْمَةً وَّعِلْمًا فَاغْفِرْ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْا سَبِيْلَكَ وَقِهِمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(7)\nLAZEENA YAHMELOONA AL-A’ARSHA WA MAN HAWLAHU YUSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA YOAMENOONA BEHI WAYASTAGHFEROONA LILLAZEENA AAMANOO RABBANAA WASEA’TA KULLA SHAY-IN RAHMATAM WA I’LMAA FAGH-FIR LILLAZEENA TAABOO WAT TABA-O’O SABEELAKA WAQEHEM A’ZAABAL JAHEEM.\nThose who sustain the Throne (of Allah) and those around it Sing Glory and Praise to their Lord; believe in Him; and implore Forgiveness for those who believe: “Our Lord! Thy Reach is over all things, in Mercy and Knowledge. Forgive, then, those who turn in Repentance, and follow Thy Path; and preserve them from the Penalty of the Blazing Fire! \nرَبَّنَا وَاَدْخِلْهُمْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنِ اۨلَّتِىْ وَعَدْتَّهُمْ وَمَنْ صَلَحَ مِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَاَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ ۙ‏(8)\nRABBANAA WAADKHELHUM JANNATIN A’ADNE LATEE WAA’ADTTAHUM WA MAN SALAHA MIN AAABAAEHEM WA AZWAAJEHIM WAZURREETEHEM INNAKA ANTA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\n“And grant, our Lord! that they enter the Gardens of Eternity, which Thou hast promised to them, and to the righteous among their fathers, their wives, and their posterity! For Thou art (He), the Exalted in Might, Full of Wisdom. \nوَقِهِمُ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ وَمَنْ تَقِ السَّيِّاٰتِ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَقَدْ رَحِمْتَهٗ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(9)\nWAQEHEMU SAYYE-AATE WA MAN TAQE SAYYE-AATE YAWMA-EZIN FAQAD RAHEMTAH WAZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\n“And preserve them from (all) ills; and any whom Thou dost preserve from ills that Day, on them wilt Thou have bestowed Mercy indeed: and that will be truly (for them) the highest Achievement”. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُنَادَوْنَ لَمَقْتُ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ مَّقْتِكُمْ اَنْفُسَكُمْ اِذْ تُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى الْاِيْمَانِ فَتَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YONAADAWNA LAMAQTU LAAHE AKBARO MIM MMAQTEKUM ANFOSAKUM IZ TUDA’AWNA ELAL AL-AEEMAANE FA TAKFOROONA.\nThe Unbelievers will be addressed: “Greater was the aversion of Allah to you than (is) your aversion to yourselves, seeing that ye were called to the Faith and ye used to refuse.” \nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اَمَتَّنَا اثْنَتَيْنِ وَاَحْيَيْتَنَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فَاعْتَرَفْنَا بِذُنُوْبِنَا فَهَلْ اِلٰى خُرُوْجٍ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍ‏(11)\nQAALOO RABBANAA AAMATTANAA ASNATAYNE WAAHYAYTANAA ASNATAYNE FAAA’TARAFNAA BEZUNOOBENAA FA HAL ELAA KHUROOJIN MIN SABEELIN.\nThey will say: “Our Lord! twice hast Thou made us without life, and twice hast Thou given us Life! Now have we recognised our sins: Is there any way out (of this)?” \nذٰ لِكُمْ بِاَنَّهٗۤ اِذَا دُعِىَ اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ كَفَرْتُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ يُّشْرَكْ بِهٖ تُؤْمِنُوْا ؕ فَالْحُكْمُ لِلّٰهِ الْعَلِىِّ الْكَبِيْرِ‏(12)\nZAA ZAALEKUM BE-ANNAHU EZAA DUE’EAAA LAAHO WAHDAH KAFARTUM WA YYUSHRAK BEHI LAM TOAMENOO FA HUKMO LILLAAHE AL-A’ALEAAAE AL-KABEERE.\n(The answer will be:) “This is because, when Allah was invoked as the Only (object of worship), ye did reject Faith, but when partners were joined to Him, ye believed! the Command is with Allah, Most High, Most Great!” \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ وَيُنَزِّلُ لَكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ رِزْقًا ؕ وَمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اِلَّا مَنْ يُّنِيْبُ‏(13)\nHOWA LAZEE YUREEKUM AAYAATEHI WAYUNAZZELU LAKUM MENAL SAMAAA-E RIZQAN WA MAA YATAZAKKARU ILLAA MAN YYUNEEBU.\nHe it is Who showeth you his Signs, and sendeth down sustenance for you from the sky: but only those receive admonition who turn (to Allah). \nفَادْعُوا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nFAADU’OOA LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUL DEENA WA LAW KAREHA KAAFEROON.\nCall ye, then, upon Allah with sincere devotion to Him, even though the Unbelievers may detest it. \nرَفِيْعُ الدَّرَجٰتِ ذُو الْعَرْشِ‌ ۚ يُلْقِى الرُّوْحَ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ لِيُنْذِرَ يَوْمَ التَّلَاقِ ۙ‏(15)\nRAFEEU’U AD-DARAJAATE ZUL A’RSHIL YULQEAA AR-ROOHA MIN AMREHI A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI LEENZERA YAWMA AT-TALAAQE.\nRaised high above ranks (or degrees), (He is) the Lord of the Throne (of Authority): by His Command doth He send the Spirit (of inspiration) to any of His servants he pleases, that it may warn (men) of the Day of Mutual Meeting, \nيَوْمَ هُمْ بَارِزُوْنَ ۚ لَا يَخْفٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْهُمْ شَىْءٌ ؕ لِمَنِ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ ؕ لِلّٰهِ الْوَاحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ‏(16)\nYAWMA HUM BAAREZOONA LAA YAKHFAA A’LAL LAAHE MINHUM SHAY-UN LEMANIT A’LAYNAA YAWMA LILLAAHE AL-WAAHEDE AL-QAHHAARE.\nThe Day whereon they will (all) come forth: not a single thing concerning them is hidden from Allah. Whose will be the dominion that Day?” That of Allah, the One the Irresistible! \nاَ لْيَوْمَ تُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ ؕ لَا ظُلْمَ الْيَوْمَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(17)\nAL-YAWMA TUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT LAA ZULMA YAWMA INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThat Day will every soul be requited for what it earned; no injustice will there be that Day, for Allah is Swift in taking account. \nوَاَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْاٰزِفَةِ اِذِ الْقُلُوْبُ لَدَى الْحَنَاجِرِ كٰظِمِيْنَ ؕ مَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٍ يُّطَاعُ ؕ‏(18)\nWAANZERHUM YAWMA AL-AAAZEFATE EZIM BALAGHATIL LADAA AL-HANAAJERE KAAZEMEENA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN HAMEEMIN WA LAA SHAFEEA’IN YYUTAAU’U.\nWarn them of the Day that is (ever) drawing near, when the hearts will (come) right up to the throats to choke (them); No intimate friend nor intercessor will the wrong-doers have, who could be listened to. \nيَعْلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَمَا تُخْفِى الصُّدُوْرُ‏(19)\nYA’LAMO KHAAENATA AL-AAA’YUNE WA MAA TUKHFEAA AS-SUDOORU.\n(Allah) knows of (the tricks) that deceive with the eyes, and all that the hearts (of men) conceal. \nوَاللّٰهُ يَقْضِىْ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَقْضُوْنَ بِشَىْءٍؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(20)\nWAL LAAHO YAQZEE BIL-HAQ WAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI LAA YAQZOONA BE-SHAYIN INNAL LAAHA HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nAnd Allah will judge with (justice and) Truth: but those whom (men) invoke besides Him, will not (be in a position) to judge at all. Verily it is Allah (alone) Who hears and sees (all things). \nاَوَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَشَدَّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً وَّاٰثَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّاقٍ‏(21)\nAWALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA KAANOO MIN QABLEHIM KAANOO HUM ASHADDA MINHUM QUWWAH WWAASAARAN FIL ARZE TOOFAANO LAAHO BEZUNOOBEHEM WA MAA KAANA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN WWAAQIN.\nDo they not travel through the earth and see what was the End of those before them? They were even superior to them in strength, and in the traces (they have left) in the land: but Allah did call them to account for their sins, and none had they to defend them against Allah. \nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانَتْ تَّاْتِيْهِمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَكَفَرُوْا فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّهٗ قَوِىٌّ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(22)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAANAT TTAATEEHEM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FA KAFAROO TOOFAANO LAAH INNAHU QAWEAAAUN SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nThat was because there came to them their messengers with Clear (Signs), but they rejected them: So Allah called them to account: for He is Full of Strength, Strict in Punishment. \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA WASULTAANIN MOBEEN.\nOf old We sent Moses, with Our Signs and an authority manifest, \nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَ هَامٰنَ وَقَارُوْنَ فَقَالُوْا سٰحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ‏(24)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAANA WA QAAROONA FA-QAALOO SAAHERUN KAZZAABUN.\nTo Pharaoh, Haman, and Qarun; but they called (him)” a sorcerer telling lies!”... \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْا اقْتُلُوْۤا اَبْنَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ وَاسْتَحْيُوْا نِسَآءَهُمْؕ وَمَا كَيْدُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(25)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM BIL-HAQQE MIN I’NDENAA QAALOO AQTULOOA AABNAAA LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU WAASTAHYOOA NESAAAHUM WA MAA KAYDU KAAFEREEN ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM.\nNow, when he came to them in Truth, from Us, they said, “Slay the sons of those who believe with him, and keep alive their females,” but the plots of Unbelievers (end) in nothing but errors (and delusions)!... \nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ ذَرُوْنِىْۤ اَقْتُلْ مُوْسٰى وَلْيَدْعُ رَبَّهٗ‌ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّبَدِّلَ دِيْنَكُمْ اَوْ اَنْ يُّظْهِرَ فِى الْاَرْضِ الْفَسَادَ‏(26)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO ZAROONEAA AAQTUL MOOSAA WALYADU’U WAL INNEE AKHAAFO AN YYUBADDELA DEENAKUM AW AN YYUZHERA FIL ARZE FASAADA.\nSaid Pharaoh: “Leave me to slay Moses; and let him call on his Lord! What I fear is lest he should change your religion, or lest he should cause mischief to appear in the land!” \nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اِنِّىْ عُذْتُ بِرَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ مُتَكَبِّرٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِيَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ‏(27)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA INNEE U’ZTO BE-RABBEE WA RABBEKUM MIN KULLE MUTAKABBERIN LAA BIL LAAHE BE-YAWMID HESAAB.\nMoses said: “I have indeed called upon my Lord and your Lord (for protection) from every arrogant one who believes not in the Day of Account!” \nوَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ ‌ۖ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَكْتُمُ اِيْمَانَهٗۤ اَتَقْتُلُوْنَ رَجُلًا اَنْ يَّقُوْلَ رَبِّىَ اللّٰهُ وَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّكُ كَاذِبًا فَعَلَيْهِ كَذِبُهٗ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّكُ صَادِقًا يُّصِبْكُمْ بَعْضُ الَّذِىْ يَعِدُكُمْ ۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ كَذَّابٌ‏(28)\nWA QAALA RAJOLUM MOAMENUN MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YAKTUMU AEEMAANAH AATAQTULOONA RAJULAN AN YAQOOLA RABBEYAL LAAHO WA QAD JAAA-AKUM BIL-BAYYENAATE MIR RABBEKUM WA YYAKU KAAZEBAN FA-A’LAYHE KAZEBUH WA YYAKU SAADEQAN YYUSEBKUM BA’ZUL LAZEE YA-E’DOKUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN HOWA MUSREFUN KAZZAABUN.\nA believer, a man from among the people of Pharaoh, who had concealed his faith, said: “Will ye slay a man because he says, 'My Lord is Allah'? when he has indeed come to you with Clear (Signs) from your Lord? and if he be a liar, on him is (the sin of) his lie: but, if he is telling the Truth, then will fall on you something of the (calamity) of which he warns you: Truly Allah guides not one who transgresses and lies! \nيٰقَوْمِ لَكُمُ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ ظٰهِرِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَمَنْ يَّنْصُرُنَا مِنْۢ بَاْسِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ جَآءَنَا ؕ قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ مَاۤ اُرِيْكُمْ اِلَّا مَاۤ اَرٰى وَمَاۤ اَهْدِيْكُمْ اِلَّا سَبِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ‏(29)\nLE-QAWMEHI LAKOMUL A’LAYNAA YAWMA ZAAHEREENA FIL ARZE FAMAN YYANSURUNAA MIN BAASE LAAHE IN JAAA-ANAA QAALA FIRA’WNO MAA AUREEKUM ILLAA MAA AARAA WA MAA AAHDEEKUM ILLAA SABEELA AR-RASHAADE.\n“O my People! Yours is the dominion this day: Ye have the upper hand in the land: but who will help us from the Punishment of Allah, should it befall us?” Pharaoh said: “I but point out to you that which I see (myself); Nor do I guide you but to the Path of Right!” \nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَ يٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّثْلَ يَوْمِ الْاَحْزَابِۙ‏(30)\nWA QAALA LAZEE AAMANA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM MISLA YAWMIL AL-AAHZAABE.\nThen said the man who believed: “O my people! Truly I do fear for you something like the Day (of disaster) of the Confederates (in sin)!- \nمِثْلَ دَاْبِ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ ظُلْمًا لِّلْعِبَادِ‏(31)\nMISLA DAABE QAWME NOOHIN WWAA’AADIN WA WAL LAZEENA MIN BAA’DEHEM WA MAA LAAHO YOREEDO ZULMAWN LLELE’EBAADE.\n“Something like the fate of the People of Noah, the 'Ad, and the Thamud, and those who came after them: but Allah never wishes injustice to his Servants. \nوَيٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَوْمَ التَّنَادِۙ‏(32)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM YAWMA AT-TANAADE.\n“And O my people! I fear for you a Day when there will be Mutual calling (and wailing), \nيَوْمَ تُوَلُّوْنَ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‌ۚ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ عَاصِمٍۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(33)\nYAWMA TOOLLOONA MUDBEREEN MAA LAKUM MENAL LAAHE MIN A’AASEMIN WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\n“A Day when ye shall turn your backs and flee: No defender shall ye have from Allah: Any whom Allah leaves to stray, there is none to guide... \nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ يُوْسُفُ مِنْ قَبْلُ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَمَا زِلْتُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا جَآءَكُمْ بِهٖ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا هَلَكَ قُلْتُمْ لَنْ يَّبْعَثَ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ رَسُوْلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ مُّرْتَابٌ  ۚ ۖ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AKUM YOOSUFU MIN QABLO BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA ZELTUM FEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA JAAA-AKUM BEHI HATTAA EZAA HALAKA IZ QULTUM LAN YYABA’ASA LAAHO MIN BA’DEHI RASOOLAM KAZAALEKA YOZILLO LAAHO MAN HOWA MUSREFUN MMURTAABUN.\n“And to you there came Joseph in times gone by, with Clear Signs, but ye ceased not to doubt of the (Mission) for which he had come: At length, when he died, ye said: 'No messenger will Allah send after him.' thus doth Allah leave to stray such as transgress and live in doubt, \nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ سُلْطٰنٍ اَتٰٮهُمْ ؕ كَبُرَ مَقْتًا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَطْبَعُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ قَلْبِ مُتَكَبِّرٍ جَبَّارٍ‏(35)\nLAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL SULTAANIN ATAAHUM KABURA MAQTAN I’NDAL LAAHE WA I’NDAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KAZAALEKA YATBA-U’L LAAHO A’LAA KULLE QALBE MUTAKABBERIN JABBAARIN.\n“(Such) as dispute about the Signs of Allah, without any authority that hath reached them, grievous and odious (is such conduct) in the sight of Allah and of the Believers. Thus doth Allah, seal up every heart - of arrogant and obstinate Transgressors.” \nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يٰهَامٰنُ ابْنِ لِىْ صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَبْلُغُ الْاَسْبَابَۙ‏(36)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO YAAHAAMAANO MARYAM LEE SARHAL LA-A’LLEE AABLUGHU AL-AASBAABA.\nPharaoh said: “O Haman! Build me a lofty palace, that I may attain the ways and means- \nاَسْبَابَ السَّمٰوٰتِ فَاَطَّلِعَ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِ مُوْسٰى وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّهٗ كَاذِبًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِفِرْعَوْنَ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِهٖ وَصُدَّ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ ؕ وَمَا كَيْدُ فِرْعَوْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ تَبَابٍ‏(37)\nAASBAABA SAMAAWAATE FAATTALEA’A ELAA ELAAHE MOOSAA WA INNEE LA-AZUNNOHU KAAZEBAN WA KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LE-FIR-A’WNA SOOO-UL A’AMALEH WASUDDA A’NIL SABEELE WA MAA KAYDU FIR-A’WNA ILLAA FEE TABAABIN.\n“The ways and means of (reaching) the heavens, and that I may mount up to the god of Moses: But as far as I am concerned, I think (Moses) is a liar!” Thus was made alluring, in Pharaoh's eyes, the evil of his deeds, and he was hindered from the Path; and the plot of Pharaoh led to nothing but perdition (for him). \nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَ يٰقَوْمِ اتَّبِعُوْنِ اَهْدِكُمْ سَبِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ‌ۚ‏(38)\nWA QAALA LAZEE AAMANA LE-QAWMEHI ATTABEU’OONE AAHDEKUM SABEELA AR-RASHAADE.\nThe man who believed said further: “O my people! Follow me: I will lead you to the Path of Right. \nيٰقَوْمِ اِنَّمَا هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا مَتَاعٌ وَّاِنَّ الْاٰخِرَةَ هِىَ دَارُ الْقَرَارِ‏(39)\nLE-QAWMEHI INNAMAA HAAZEHE HAYAATUD DUNYAA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE WWAANNA AAKHERATA HEYA DAARU AL-QARAARE.\n“O my people! This life of the present is nothing but (temporary) convenience: It is the Hereafter that is the Home that will last. \nمَنْ عَمِلَ سَيِّئَةً فَلَا يُجْزٰٓى اِلَّا مِثْلَهَا ۚ وَمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ يُرْزَقُوْنَ فِيْهَا بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(40)\nMAN A’MELA SAYYE-ATANW FALAA YUJZAAA ILLAA MESLAHAA WA MAN A’MELA SAALEHAN MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA YURZAQOONA FEEHAA BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\n“He that works evil will not be requited but by the like thereof: and he that works a righteous deed - whether man or woman - and is a Believer- such will enter the Garden (of Bliss): Therein will they have abundance without measure. \nوَيٰقَوْمِ مَا لِىْۤ اَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى النَّجٰوةِ وَتَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَى النَّارِؕ‏(41)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI MAA LEE AADU’OOKUM ELAL AN-NAJAAWTE WATADU’OONANEAA ELAL NAAR.\n“And O my people! How (strange) it is for me to call you to Salvation while ye call me to the Fire! \nتَدْعُوْنَنِىْ لِاَكْفُرَ بِاللّٰهِ وَاُشْرِكَ بِهٖ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ وَّاَنَا اَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى الْعَزِيْزِ الْغَفَّارِ‏(42)\nTADU’OONANEAA LEAAKFURA BIL-LAAHE WAASHREKA BEHI MAA LAYSA LEE BEHI I’LMUM WWAANAA AADU’OOKUM ELAL A’ZEEZIL AL-GHAFFAARE.\n“Ye do call upon me to blaspheme against Allah, and to join with Him partners of whom I have no knowledge; and I call you to the Exalted in Power, Who forgives again and again!” \nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّمَا تَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ لَيْسَ لَهٗ دَعْوَةٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَلَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَنَّ مَرَدَّنَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَاَنَّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ هُمْ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ‏(43)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAMAA TADU’OONANEAA ELAYHE LAYSA LAHU DAA’WATUN FIL DUNYAA WA LAA FIL AAKHERATE WA ANNAL MARADDANAA ELAL LAAHE WA ANNAL MUSREFEEN HUM ASHAABUN NAAR.\n“Without doubt ye do call me to one who is not fit to be called to, whether in this world, or in the Hereafter; our return will be to Allah; and the Transgressors will be Companions of the Fire! \nفَسَتَذْكُرُوْنَ مَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْؕ وَاُفَوِّضُ اَمْرِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِالْعِبَادِ‏(44)\nFASATAZKUROONA MAA AAQOOLU LAKUM WAAFAWZU AMREE ELAL LAAH INNAL LAAHA BASEER BIL-E'BAAD.\n“Soon will ye remember what I say to you (now), My (own) affair I commit to Allah: for Allah (ever) watches over His Servants.” \nفَوَقٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ سَيِّاٰتِ مَا مَكَرُوْا وَحَاقَ بِاٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ سُوْٓءُ الْعَذَابِ‌ۚ‏(45)\nFAWAQAAHU LAAHO SAYAAATE MAA MAKAROOA WAHAAQA BE-AALE FIR-A’WNA SOOO-UL A’ZAABE.\nThen Allah saved him from (every) ill that they plotted (against him), but the burnt of the Penalty encompassed on all sides the People of Pharaoh. \nاَلنَّارُ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا غُدُوًّا وَّعَشِيًّا ۚ وَيَوْمَ تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ اَدْخِلُوْۤا اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ اَشَدَّ الْعَذَابِ‏(46)\nAALNNAARU YUA’RAZOONA A’LAYHAA GHUDOOA WWAA’ASHEEA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUS SAA-A’TO AADKHELOOA AALA FIR-A’WNA ASHADDA A’ZAABE.\nIn front of the Fire will they be brought, morning and evening: And (the sentence will be) on the Day that Judgment will be established: “Cast ye the People of Pharaoh into the severest Penalty!” \nوَاِذْ يَتَحَآجُّوْنَ فِى النَّارِ فَيَقُوْلُ الضُّعَفٰٓؤُا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا لَكُمْ تَبَعًا فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّغْنُوْنَ عَنَّا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ النَّارِ‏(47)\nWA IZ YATAHAAJJOONA FIL NAAR FAYAQOOLO AZ-ZUA’AFAAAUA LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA KUNNAA LAKUM TABAA’AN FA HAL ANTUM MMUGHNOONA WAGH NASEEBAN MENAL NAAR.\nBehold, they will dispute with each other in the Fire! The weak ones (who followed) will say to those who had been arrogant, “We but followed you: Can ye then take (on yourselves) from us some share of the Fire? \nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُلٌّ فِيْهَاۤۙاِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ حَكَمَ بَيْنَ الْعِبَادِ‏(48)\nQAALAL LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA KULLUL FEEHAAAENNA LAAHA QAD HAKAMA BAYNA A’LAL.\nThose who had been arrogant will say: “We are all in this (Fire)! Truly, Allah has judged between (his) Servants!” \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ فِى النَّارِ لِخَزَنَةِ جَهَنَّمَ ادْعُوْا رَبَّكُمْ يُخَفِّفْ عَنَّا يَوْمًا مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ‏(49)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA FIL NAAR LEKHAZANATE JAHANNAMA O’O TAQUL YUKHAFFEF WAGH YAWMAN MENAL A’ZAABE.\nThose in the Fire will say to the Keepers of Hell: “Pray to your Lord to lighten us the Penalty for a day (at least)!” \nقَالُوْۤا اَوَلَمْ تَكُ تَاْتِيْكُمْ رُسُلُكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى ؕ قَالُوْا‌ فَادْعُوْا ۚ وَمَا دُعٰٓؤُا الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(50)\nQAALOO AWALAM TAKU TAATEEKUM RUSULUKUM BIL-BAYYENAATE QAALOO BALAA QAALOO FA O’O WA MAA DUA’AAAUA KAAFEREEN ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM.\nThey will say: “Did there not come to you your messengers with Clear Signs?” They will say, “Yes”. They will reply, “Then pray (as ye like)! But the prayer of those without Faith is nothing but (futile wandering) in (mazes of) error!” \nاِنَّا لَنَنْصُرُ رُسُلَنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَيَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الْاَشْهَادُ ۙ‏(51)\nINNAA LANANSURU RUSULANAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUL AL-AASHHAADU.\nWe will, without doubt, help our messengers and those who believe, (both) in this world's life and on the Day when the Witnesses will stand forth, \nيَوْمَ لَا يَنْفَعُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ مَعْذِرَتُهُمْ وَلَهُمُ اللَّعْنَةُ وَلَهُمْ سُوْٓءُ الدَّارِ‏(52)\nYAWMA LAA YANFAU’N ZAALEMEEN MA’ZERATOHUM WA LAHOMUL AL-LAA’NATU WA LAHUM SOOO-UL AD-DAARE.\nThe Day when no profit will it be to Wrong-doers to present their excuses, but they will (only) have the Curse and the Home of Misery. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْهُدٰى وَاَوْرَثْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْكِتٰبَۙ‏(53)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL HODAA WAAWRASNAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KETAABA.\nWe did aforetime give Moses the (Book of) Guidance, and We gave the book in inheritance to the Children of Israel, \nهُدًى وَّذِكْرٰى لِاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(54)\nHODAM WA ZIKRAA LE-ULIL ULIL ALBAABE.\nA Guide and a Message to men of Understanding. \nفَاصْبِرْ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّاسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنْۢبِكَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ بِالْعَشِىِّ وَالْاِبْكَارِ‏(55)\nFAS-BIR INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WWAASTAGHFER LE-ZAMBEKA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA BIL-A’ASHEAAAE WAL AEBKAARE.\nPatiently, then, persevere: for the Promise of Allah is true: and ask forgiveness for thy fault, and celebrate the Praises of thy Lord in the evening and in the morning. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ سُلْطٰنٍ اَتٰٮهُمْۙ اِنْ فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ اِلَّا كِبْرٌ مَّا هُمْ بِبَالِغِيْهِؕ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(56)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL SULTAANIN ATAAHUM IN FEE SODOOREHIM ILLAA KEBRUN MAA HUM BEBAALEGHEEHE FAS-TA-I’Z BILLAAH INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nThose who dispute about the signs of Allah without any authority bestowed on them, there is nothing in their breasts but (the quest of) greatness, which they shall never attain to: seek refuge, then, in Allah: It is He Who hears and sees (all things). \nلَخَلْقُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ خَلْقِ النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(57)\nLAKHALQU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE AKBARO MIN KHALQIS NAASE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAssuredly the creation of the heavens and the earth is a greater (matter) than the creation of men: Yet most men understand not. \nوَمَا يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَلَا الْمُسِىْٓءُ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA MAA YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA LAA AL-MUSEAAAAU QALEELAA MAA TATAZAKKAROONA.\nNot equal are the blind and those who (clearly) see: Nor are (equal) those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, and those who do evil. Little do ye learn by admonition! \nاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَاٰتِيَةٌ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(59)\nINNAL SAA-A’TA LAATEETUN LAA RAYBA FEEHAA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOON.\nThe Hour will certainly come: Therein is no doubt: Yet most men believe not. \nوَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُوْنِىْۤ اَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِىْ سَيَدْخُلُوْنَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِيْنَ‏(60)\nWA QAALA RABBUKUMU ADU’OONEAA AASTAJEB LAKUM INNAL LAZEENA YASTAKBEROONA A’N E’EBAADATEAA SA-YADKHOLOONA JAHANNAMA DAAKHEREENA.\nAnd your Lord says: “Call on Me; I will answer your (Prayer): but those who are too arrogant to serve Me will surely find themselves in Hell - in humiliation!” \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَ لٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(61)\nALLAAHO LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LETASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAN INNAL LAAHA LAZOO FAZLIN A’LAL NAASE WA LAAKENNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YASHKOROON.\nIt is Allah Who has made the Night for you, that ye may rest therein, and the days as that which helps (you) to see. Verily Allah is full of Grace and Bounty to men: yet most men give no thanks. \nذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ‌ ۘ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ‌ۚ  فَاَ نّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(62)\nZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA-ANNAA TUFAKOONA.\nSuch is Allah, your Lord, the Creator of all things, there is no god but He: Then how ye are deluded away from the Truth! \nكَذٰلِكَ يُؤْفَكُ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(63)\nKAZAALEKA YUFAKU LAZEENA KAANOO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nThus are deluded those who are wont to reject the Signs of Allah. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ قَرَارًا وَّالسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَّصَوَّرَكُمْ فَاَحْسَنَ صُوَرَكُمْ وَرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ ‌ ۖۚ فَتَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(64)\nALLAAHO LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA QARAARAWN WAS SAMAAA-A BENAAA-ANW WWASAWRAKUM FA AHSANAL SOORAKUM WARAZAQAKUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM FA TABAARAKAS-MO LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nIt is Allah Who has made for you the earth as a resting place, and the sky as a canopy, and has given you shape- and made your shapes beautiful, and has provided for you Sustenance, of things pure and good;- such is Allah your Lord. So Glory to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds! \nهُوَ الْحَىُّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ فَادْعُوْهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَؕ اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(65)\nHOWA HAYYUL LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FAADU’OOHU MUKHLESEENA LAHUL AD-DEENA AALHAMDU LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nHe is the Living (One): There is no god but He: Call upon Him, giving Him sincere devotion. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds! \nقُلْ اِنِّىْ نُهِيْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَمَّا جَآءَنِىَ الْبَيِّنٰتُ مِنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اُسْلِمَ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(66)\nQUL INNEE NUHEETU AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAMMAA JAAANEAAA BAYYENAATO MIR A-A’LAMO WA AN A-A’BODA AN AUSLEMA LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSay: “I have been forbidden to invoke those whom ye invoke besides Allah, seeing that the Clear Signs have come to me from my Lord; and I have been commanded to bow (in Islam) to the Lord of the Worlds.” \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ عَلَقَةٍ ثُمَّ يُخْرِجُكُمْ طِفْلًا ثُمَّ لِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَشُدَّكُمْ ثُمَّ لِتَكُوْنُوْا شُيُوْخًا ؕ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّتَوَفّٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَجَلًا مُّسَمًّى وَّلَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nHOWA LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA MIN A’ALAQATIN SUMMA YUKHREJUKUM TEFLAN SUMMA LETABLUGHOOA AASHUDDAKUM SUMMA LE-TAKOONOO SHUYOOKHAN WA MINKUM MAN YYUTAWAFFAA MIN QABLO WALETABLUGHOOA AAJALAN AJALIM WWALAA’ALLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nIt is He Who has created you from dust then from a sperm-drop, then from a leech-like clot; then does he get you out (into the light) as a child: then lets you (grow and) reach your age of full strength; then lets you become old, though of you there are some who die before;- and lets you reach a Term appointed; in order that ye may learn wisdom. \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ فَاِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(68)\nHOWA LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEET FA-EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nIt is He Who gives Life and Death; and when He decides upon an affair, He says to it, “Be”, and it is. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِؕ اَنّٰى يُصْرَفُوْنَ  ۛۚ ۙ‏(69)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAH ANNAA YUSRAFOONA.\nSeest thou not those that dispute concerning the Signs of Allah? How are they turned away (from Reality)? \nالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْكِتٰبِ وَبِمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا بِهٖ رُسُلَنَا ۛ  فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ‏(70)\nLAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-KETAABE WA BEMAA ARSALNAA BEHI RUSULANAA FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nThose who reject the Book and the (revelations) with which We sent our messengers: but soon shall they know, \nاِذِ الْاَغْلٰلُ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِهِمْ وَالسَّلٰسِلُؕ يُسْحَبُوْنَۙ‏(71)\nEZIM AL-AAGHLAALU FEE AAA’NAAQEHEM WAALSSALAASELU YUSHABOONA.\nWhen the yokes (shall be) round their necks, and the chains; they shall be dragged along- \nفِى الْحَمِيْمِ ۙ ثُمَّ فِى النَّارِ يُسْجَرُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(72)\nFIL HAMEEM SUMMA FIL NAAR YUSJAROONA.\nIn the boiling fetid fluid: then in the Fire shall they be burned; \nثُمَّ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(73)\nSUMMA QEELA LAHUM AYNA MAA KUNTUM TUSHREKOONA.\nThen shall it be said to them: “Where are the (deities) to which ye gave part-worship- \nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ قَالُوْا ضَلُّوْا عَنَّا بَلْ لَّمْ نَكُنْ نَّدْعُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ شَيْئًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(74)\nMIN DOONIL LAAHE QAALOO ZALLOOA WAGH BAL LAM NAKUN NNADU’OOA MIN QABLO SHAY-ANW KAZAALEKA YOZILLO LAAHO KAAFEREEN.\n“In derogation of Allah?” They will reply: “They have left us in the lurch: Nay, we invoked not, of old, anything (that had real existence).” Thus does Allah leave the Unbelievers to stray. \nذٰ لِكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَفْرَحُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَمْرَحُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(75)\nZAA ZAALEKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TAFRAHOON FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA BEMAA KUNTUM TAMRAHOONA.\n“That was because ye were wont to rejoice on the earth in things other than the Truth, and that ye were wont to be insolent. \nاُدْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ۚ فَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(76)\nAUDKHULOOA AABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA FA MASALUL MASWAA AL-MUTAKABBEREENA.\n“Enter ye the gates of Hell, to dwell therein: and evil is (this) abode of the arrogant!” \nفَاصْبِرْ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّۚ فَاِمَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(77)\nFAS-BIR INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN FA-IMMAA NUREENNAKA YAWM LAZEE NAE’EDUHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA ELAYNAA YARJEO’ON.\nSo persevere in patience; for the Promise of Allah is true: and whether We show thee (in this life) some part of what We promise them, or We take thy soul (to Our Mercy) (before that), (in any case) it is to Us that they shall (all) return. \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْهُمْ مَّنْ قَصَصْنَا عَلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ لَّمْ نَقْصُصْ عَلَيْكَؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِرَسُوْلٍ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِاٰيَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰه‌ِۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ قُضِىَ بِالْحَقِّ وَخَسِرَ هُنَالِكَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ROSOLAN MIN QABLEKA MINHUM MAN QASASNAA A’LAYKA WA MINHUM MAN LAM NAQSUS A’LAYK WA MAA KAANA LE-RASOOLIN AN YAATEYA BE-AAYATIL ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAHE FA-EZAA JAAA-A AMRUL LAAHE QUZEAAA BIL-HAQQE WAKHASERA HONAALEKAB MUBTELOON.\nWe did aforetime send messengers before thee: of them there are some whose story We have related to thee, and some whose story We have not related to thee. It was not (possible) for any messenger to bring a sign except by the leave of Allah: but when the Command of Allah issued, the matter was decided in truth and justice, and there perished, there and then those who stood on Falsehoods. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامَ لِتَرْكَبُوْا مِنْهَا وَمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(79)\nALLAAHO LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL AL-AANA’AAMA LETARKABOOA MINHAA WA MINHAA TAAKULOONA.\nIt is Allah Who made cattle for you, that ye may use some for riding and some for food; \nوَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ وَ لِتَبْلُغُوْا عَلَيْهَا حَاجَةً فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْ وَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُوْنَؕ‏(80)\nWA LAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ WA LETABLUGHOOA A’LAYHAA HAAJATAM FEE SUDOOREKUM MAKTASABAT RABBANAA WA FULKE TUHMALOONA.\nAnd there are (other) advantages in them for you (besides); that ye may through them attain to any need (there may be) in your hearts; and on them and on ships ye are carried. \nوَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ ۖ  فَاَىَّ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ تُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(81)\nYOREEKUM AAYAATEHI FAAAAAA AAYAATIL LAAHE TUNKEROONA.\nAnd He shows you (always) His Signs: then which of the Signs of Allah will ye deny? \nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَانُوْۤا اَكْثَرَ مِنْهُمْ وَاَشَدَّ قُوَّةً وَّ اٰثَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(82)\nA-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM KAANOO AKSARAN MINHUM WA ASHADDA QUWWAH WA AAASAARAN FIL ARZE FAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nDo they not travel through the earth and see what was the End of those before them? They were more numerous than these and superior in strength and in the traces (they have left) in the land: Yet all that they accomplished was of no profit to them. \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَرِحُوْا بِمَا عِنْدَهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(83)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAREHOO BEMAA E’ENDAHUM MENAL I’LME WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nFor when their messengers came to them with Clear Signs, they exulted in such knowledge (and skill) as they had; but that very (Wrath) at which they were wont to scoff hemmed them in. \nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْا بَاْسَنَا قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَحْدَهٗ وَكَفَرْنَا بِمَا كُنَّا بِهٖ مُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(84)\nFALAMMAA RA-AW BAASANAA QAALOO AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WAHDAH WAKAFARNAA BEMAA KUNNAA BEHI MUSHREKEENA.\nBut when they saw Our Punishment, they said: “We believe in Allah, the one Allah - and we reject the partners we used to join with Him.” \nفَلَمْ يَكُ يَنْفَعُهُمْ اِيْمَانُهُمْ لَمَّا رَاَوْا بَاْسَنَا ؕ سُنَّتَ اللّٰهِ الَّتِىْ قَدْ خَلَتْ فِىْ عِبَادِهٖ‌ۚ وَخَسِرَ هُنَالِكَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nFALAM YAKU YANFAU’UHUM AEEMAANUHUM LAMMAA RA-AW BAASANAA SUNNATA LAAHE LATEE QAD KHALAT FEE E’BAADEHI WAKHASERA HONAALEKAB KAAFEROON.\nBut their professing the Faith when they (actually) saw Our Punishment was not going to profit them. (Such has been) Allah's Way of dealing with His Servants (from the most ancient times). And even thus did the Rejecters of Allah perish (utterly)! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Mo’min (The Believer) Or Surah Ghaafir\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 85 verses. When a person recites this Surah then the souls of all the Prophet (a.s.), the truthful people and the believers send salutations to him and pray for his forgiveness. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah once in every three days, his sins will be forgiven and he will become a God-fearing person.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if this Surah is written and kept in a garden or farm, then the plants or crops will become more fruit bearing and green. If kept in a business premises then business will prosper and more profit will be gained. Keeping this Surah as a talisman works as a cure for wounds and scars. This Surah is also a remedy for heart problems, dizziness and nausea."
}
